ur help I need your prose and I  need some money and then I said I looked  around his office I'm like we don't even  have Tiger Woods  I could tell she was sincere and genuine  but very forward and I respected that  Kevin helm is the executive director of  the Michigan section of the PGA of  America why involve yourselves with  midnight golf this is a way that we  could try to diversify the game and get  involved to help young people in Detroit  Michigan PGA became a partner from the  very beginning and provides eight  volunteer professionals every week to  teach the kids what were you hoping to  accomplish with it my goal was to always  get kids in college the program started  in 2001 with just 17 kids today it's a  free 30 week program for 265 high school  seniors with a 2.3 million dollar budget  the kids get dinner golf instruction  small group mentorship from local  leaders and cottage counseling that  culminates with a college tour in the  spring I got accepted into Penn State  and North Carolina A&amp;T what's been the  success of sending students to college  ninety-eight percent that's higher than  the national average significantly yes  what are you guys doing giving them love  we want them to be successful dr. amber  Glenn is an example of that success she  went through the midnight golf program  in 2006 and it changed her life for me  being a participant in the midnight golf  program was an eye-opener in itself  right midnight golf said these are all  of the possibilities of things that you  could be she played golf in college and  then went on to medical school here you  can see the heart beating right here and  dr. Glenn credits miss Renee she is a  motherly figure to me she has been  personally vested in my success circle  just raised Jason Malone is now 37 and  serves on the board of midnight golf  with his mom he's overwhelmed by what  she's accomplished Detroit is a really  tough place to exist the goal of this  program was just to give him a chance it  really means a lot to to give back and  that all started with my mom  we cannot lose hope on our kids somebody  just got to believe in what they doing  if you believe they know they'd do it  since Rene Fluker started midnight golf  back in 2001 the program with support  from the PGA of America and numerous  volunteers has helped over 2,500 Detroit  students graduate high school go on to  college and some earn scholarships it  truly is a labor of ongoing love boy he  has a lot of love also known as Miss  reneik it's so true one person can make  a difference when kids think that you  care something is simple simple as a hug  or a love or a smile what a giant  accomplishment not a small difference  out there there's no that's that  changing kids lives literally I love her  son too  who's there so proud of his mom nicely  done very nicely done
 

